WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.730
<v Pledgivo>The whole install, end to end

2
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:42.730
<v Get Started>Eight rows, graded against your org — Read the evidence line under each row before you touch anything

3
00:00:42.730 --> 00:01:05.250
<v Get Started>Row 1 — give your team access — Use the row's own button; it assigns the permission set for you

4
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:23.250
<v Get Started>Row 2 — confirm the record type mapping — Check all eight rows rendered; this one is seeded by the install

5
00:01:23.250 --> 00:02:09.130
<v Get Started>Row 7 — your organization name and logo — Fill in the name donors will see; blank means blank on the public pages

6
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:30.405
<v Get Started>The optional row — content hosts — Report only: trust a host in Setup, and only the ones you use

7
00:02:30.405 --> 00:03:43.845
<v Settings>Email & Receipts — Sender, reply-to, receipt numbering and the donor-facing wording

8
00:03:43.845 --> 00:04:20.125
<v Settings>Refunds — Decide who may refund, and what happens to the gift record

9
00:04:20.125 --> 00:05:00.805
<v Settings>Recurring & Dunning — How many times a failed recurring charge is retried, and when it stops

10
00:05:00.805 --> 00:06:06.245
<v Settings>Donor Portal — What a donor can see and change about their own giving

11
00:06:06.245 --> 00:06:32.545
<v Site & Domain>Step 1 — Digital Experiences — Auto-checked: the panel can see whether it is switched on

12
00:06:32.545 --> 00:07:41.465
<v Site & Domain>Step 2 — create or choose your site — Build Your Own (LWR) — this package does not target Aura

13
00:07:41.465 --> 00:08:35.065
<v Site & Domain>Step 3 — turn on guest access — One checkbox in Experience Builder, then reload to confirm it stuck

14
00:08:35.065 --> 00:08:47.865
<v Site & Domain>Step 4 — assign the guest permission set — Fundraising Guest Donor goes onto the site's guest user

15
00:08:47.865 --> 00:09:20.265
<v Site & Domain>Step 5 — read access to Campaign — Build this one by hand: a packaged set cannot grant it

16
00:09:20.265 --> 00:11:35.425
<v Site & Domain>Step 7 — publish, then activate — Two separate actions; publishing alone leaves it Under Construction

17
00:11:35.425 --> 00:11:47.625
<v The public site>What an anonymous visitor gets — The home route, loaded in a browser with no session

18
00:11:47.625 --> 00:12:02.400
<v The public site>The donation route, before any campaign — It renders and it asks for a campaign — that is correct at this point

19
00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:30.375
<v Payments>Step 0 — collect three keys — Two restricted keys and a publishable key, all from one gateway screen

20
00:12:30.375 --> 00:12:59.125
<v Payments>Step 1 — the external credential, twice — Custom protocol; one credential for the public site, one for the back office

21
00:12:59.125 --> 00:14:41.885
<v Payments>Step 2 — the principal, and the secret — Named Principal, one authentication parameter, holding the key

22
00:14:41.885 --> 00:15:02.410
<v Payments>Step 3 — the Authorization header — A merge formula, not a value — the key never appears here

23
00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:36.850
<v Payments>Steps 4 to 6 — the named credential — Point it at the gateway, allow the package namespace, formulas on

24
00:15:36.850 --> 00:16:50.970
<v Payments>Step 7 — let your staff use it — Principal access plus User External Credential, read and create

25
00:16:50.970 --> 00:17:09.095
<v Payments>Step 8 — let your public site use it — The donor credential's permission set goes onto the guest user

26
00:17:09.095 --> 00:17:37.295
<v Payments>Step 9 — the payment account record — Name the two named credentials, paste the publishable key, choose the mode

27
00:17:37.295 --> 00:18:10.445
<v Payments>Steps 10 and 11 — the two live checks — One passed, one failed — and the failure is the point

28
00:18:10.445 --> 00:18:34.870
<v Site & Domain>The row the panel cannot fully verify — It can see a credential grant; it cannot see which credential

29
00:18:34.870 --> 00:19:34.750
<v The fundraiser>Seven steps, then publish — Basics, story, goal, then the review that publishes it

30
00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:52.670
<v The fundraiser>The donor's address for it — The slug URL, opened anonymously — no login, no preview mode

31
00:19:52.670 --> 00:20:14.545
<v The gift>An anonymous donor pays by card — Amount, details, then the gateway's own card element

32
00:20:14.545 --> 00:20:36.720
<v The gift>Confirmed on the page, recorded a moment later — The charge is immediate; the Salesforce record is written by a job

33
00:20:36.720 --> 00:21:16.480
<v On your own site>The embed snippet, and the step people forget — Add the external origin to Allowed Embed Origins first

34
00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:32.105
<v On your own site>Running on a plain external page — The widget hands the amount, name and email across to the donation page

35
00:21:32.105 --> 00:21:59.655
<v The verdict>Health Check — the package grading itself — Five green, one red — and the red one is honest

36
00:21:59.655 --> 00:22:18.215
<v The verdict>The checklist reads complete — Seven of seven required rows Done; six changed during this run

37
00:22:18.215 --> 00:22:53.375
<v Settings>Events & Ticketing — Two fields, and they only matter if you sell tickets

38
00:22:53.375 --> 00:23:18.975
<v Settings>Page Designs — Six designs ship; pick one as the fallback for campaigns with none

39
00:23:18.975 --> 00:23:37.175
<v Settings>Public Links — Every public address the org is handing out, in one list

40
00:23:37.175 --> 00:24:14.895
<v Settings>Logging — Set the level, then read the recent gateway errors below it

41
00:24:14.895 --> 00:24:33.625
<v Wrap up>A fresh org, ready to take gifts.

42
00:24:33.625 --> 00:24:59.725
<v About Pledgivo>Fundraising and donation management, native to Salesforce. Docs: pledgivo.cloudalgo.com

